# Paths excluded from Copilot analytics line counting.
#
# Syntax: one gitignore-style pattern per line; '#' starts a comment; blank
# lines are ignored. Each entry is applied as a git ':(exclude)' pathspec when
# commit line volume is measured.
#
# These patterns ADD to the collector's built-in exclusions for generated and
# vendored files (lockfiles, *.min.*, *.map, *.snap) — they do not replace them.
#
# Only deliverable code should count toward line-volume metrics. Documentation
# and design artefacts are excluded so they cannot inflate the rate; commits
# touching them still count toward the commit-based rate.

